<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10938" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conturbātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		conturbo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>disorder, confusion.</i> * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: oculorum, <i>confused,
				indistinct vision</i>, as a disease, <i><span class="en">Scrib.
				Comp. 19</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>confusion, disquiet,
				perturbation of mind</i> (rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conturbatio metus excutiens cogitata,</span>”
				<i>a fear that drives away all thought</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Tusc. 4, 8, 19</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Top. 12, 52</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mentis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Tusc. 4, 13, 30</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
